From: edgytoast <146565462+edgytoast@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Window near field: what's nearer than the glass cut, not bent; the glass at the sill, eased

What's nearer than the glass keeps its shape and is cut at the window's allowance, as a near
plane cuts; only while the glass is still on its way to a player nearer than the allowance is what's
in front of him compressed, for those frames (AURORA_MIRROR_NEAR=ease compresses always, as before;
=raw leaves it). The glass comes no farther than where the ground meets the picture's foot
(AURORA_MIRROR_MARK_SILL, at least half the focus; AURORA_MIRROR_GLASS=focus ignores it), so the
ground there never comes out in front of it. Its distance, and with it the world's scale, follows
with a time constant of a second, within 30% of its target (AURORA_MIRROR_PLANE_SECONDS), at once on
a cut or after a gap.

